 "story": "Hiring stalled. September payrolls rose just 29K against 90K expected, July and August were revised down a combined 60K, and unemployment ticked up to 4.2% (4.1% expected) \u2014 even as ADP (+90K) and initial claims (197K) looked steadier. Inflation offered relief: core PCE ran 3.0% YoY in August, under the 3.3% consensus, though benchmark revisions also pulled July down to 3.0%. Spending stayed strong (+0.9%) while income lagged (+0.2% vs +0.5%), and annual revisions lifted Q2 GDP to 2.2%. Rates remain the pressure point: the 30-yr mortgage rate jumped to 7.28% and the 10-yr sits at 5.24%, while ISM manufacturing slipped to 54.5 with prices paid surging to 77.9. The S&P 500 is up 12.8% YTD.",
